    "body": "FROM: coordinator\nTO: guardian\nTYPE: CHECKPOINT\nRE: D045: service-core B5 evidence for review, PR #276 @ 1c7bac66a3157a0620573c769de718b7a3b85e56\n\n**Please review the evidence for D045** (the service-core B5 HOLD, which also covers #271's admission). It is in [#276](https://github.com/lmmx/mibz2/pull/276), base `research/service-core-2x3`, head `1c7bac66`, branched from the measured 3e201246. The note is `docs/journal/2026-11-09-service-core-b5-evidence.md`. CI was still running on the head when I sent this.\n\n- **Fuzz, pass A at 7e403c8e:** svc2's `2x3 + 2 in 8` and other service candidates, run through `BzReader::parallel_service`. 15,532 service cases, 0 failures. Each case is held to the plain parallel decoder (bytes, plus the error's kind, block and bit) and to libbzip2. Reach is counted from trace marks:\n  - pooled helper build and walk: 10,870;\n  - service finishing step: 13,236;\n  - back-set reuse: 5,650;\n  - front-set reuse: 3,662.\n- **Fuzz, pass B at e64469f6 (#271's admission):** run with an overlay patch; the patch is committed. 7,619 cases, 5,340 reached, 0 failures, at L = 2, 3 and 4. The prepared queue's longest was L + K − 1, observed. Pass B must be re-run if #271's `src/` changes.\n- **Mutants:** 16 hand-made, 14 killed. The two survivors are argued equivalent:\n  - H3: every build clears the table and checks each slot;\n  - O3: results are keyed by place.\n  - W2 (`notify_one`) and R3, R4 and R5 (sets lost on panic or cancel) are killed *only* by the two new lib tests.\n- **The park handshake:** `miri_a_parked_service_worker_wakes_on_the_pop` asserts, under the hub's lock, that both the worker and a team are parked before the pop. The baseline passes 20/20 and under Miri; W1 and W2 each fail it 20/20 and under Miri. The schedule it can't control is a spurious wake-up.\n- **Miri:** `service_tests::miri_*` passes 4/4.\n- **Your decision is needed on one point.**\n  - **The change:** `src/read.rs` gains a production unwind guard in the parallel `BzReader`'s feeder. A panicking source's `read` now cancels the decode and gives the reader an `io::Error`; on a normal exit it costs one `thread::panicking()` check per reader. Test `a_panicking_source`; mutant P1 is killed.\n  - **Why it matters:** that guard is on the measured `parallel_service` path. Merging #276 into `research/service-core-2x3` would make that branch's `src/` differ from the measured 3e201246.\n  - **Question:** do you want the guard here, or as a separate safety PR to master's `BzReader`, with #276 limited to test-only changes?\n- **Not covered:**\n  - aborts, OOM, and a `read` that blocks for ever (documented scope);\n  - sampled schedules on 4 cores, not an interleaving proof.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
